{"type":"agent_end","messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Using this dataset's total farmers markets, and the census file: how many farmers markets does the U.S. have per 100,000 residents, to four decimal places? One confident sentence. Do not mention unverified facts and use tools to do any math necessary. Data sources: https://harvestlymarkets.com/data/us-farmers-markets-by-state-2026.csv and https://gist.githubusercontent.com/hussainsultan/369600f5179b22792a2b4c9ed37de056/raw/NST-EST2025-ALLDATA.csv"}],"timestamp":1786917338481},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user wants me to answer: how many farmers markets does the U.S. have per 100,000 residents, to four decimal places?\n\nI need to:\n1. Use the xorq catalog to work with data\n2. Ingest the two datasets if they're not already in the catalog\n3. Calculate the ratio of farmers markets to residents and express it per 100,000\n\nLet me start by checking what's in the xorq catalog - following the instructions, I should run `xorq_semantic_models` and `xorq_catalog_list_aliases` FIRST.\n\nThe instructions say:\n- Never state a number I didn't obtain from `xorq_select`\n- Check semantic models first\n- Only ingest if no existing alias covers the data\n- For derived metrics (like ratio), compose them into the catalog\n- Use tools to do math, not my head\n- Verify every number with obligations\n\nLet me start by checking the catalog.","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"text","text":"I'll help you calculate this. Let me start by checking what's already in the xorq catalog, then ingest and process the data."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01YHSxuizGrB5HZrWQddwDYT","name":"xorq_catalog_info","arguments":{"catalog_path":".xorq/catalog"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_014isYKogUvgHLmaLfUmATSp","name":"xorq_semantic_models","arguments":{"catalog_path":".xorq/catalog"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01468zQD17kB4gEwrEk62nub","name":"xorq_catalog_list_aliases","argumen